{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL090aGVyc19MYW5ndWFnZS9GcmVuY2gtTGFuZ3VhZ2UvTGliZXJ0ZSUyMCUyODIwMTklMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Liberte","description":"1774, shortly before the French Revolution, somewhere between Potsdam and Berlin. Madame de Dumeval, the Duke de Tesis and the Duke de Wand, libertines expelled from the puritanical court of Louis XVI, seek the support of the legendary Duc de Walchen, German seducer and freethinker, lonely in a country where hypocrisy and false virtue reign. Their mission is to export libertinage, a philosophy of enlightenment founded on the rejection of moral boundaries and authorities, but moreover to find a safe place to pursue their errant games, where the quest for pleasure no longer obeys laws other than those dictated by unfulfilled desires.\n\nReleased 4 Sept 2019 · Germany, Spain · Language: French · 132 min\nStudio: Rosa Filmes, Idéale Audience, Andergraun Films","releaseInfo":"2019","genres":["Drama","History","Others"],"poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/6r9NoFRNbWMA9vXWHrgqE4wsIZp.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/4evYVAzIHXSSVFxCQhBgkgj52pH.jpg","imdbRating":"4.9","imdb_id":"tt10199670","moviedb_id":595924,"tmdbId":595924,"runtime":"132 min","cast":["Helmut Berger","Marc Susini","Laura Poulvet","Alexander García Düttmann","Lluís Serrat","Francesc Daranas","Montse Triola","Theodora Marcade"],"director":["Albert Serra"],"writer":["Albert Serra"],"released":"2019-09-04T00:00:00.000Z","country":"Germany, Spain, France","language":"French","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Albert Serra","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/4ubbOopSH7dmxTuT9v7UkMOIXPy.jpg"},{"name":"Helmut Berger","character":"Duke of Walchen","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/qcg8cIVu1gjX4FR5Y9C4QFEGX7u.jpg"},{"name":"Marc Susini","character":"Count de Tesis","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/mPVLWY7Yq2r54WiNBrjBddx3khW.jpg"},{"name":"Laura Poulvet","character":"M